s WAIT after barrier, the original WAIT print was misleading—it actually indicates post-barrier lock attempt. Moving barrier before any lock prevents pre-barrier lock hold.\", \"expected_effect\": \"Threads synchronize at barrier without holding any locks, eliminating hold-and-wait during barrier wait. After barrier, lock acquisition may still race but without pre-held locks during synchronization, avoiding the observed deadlock pattern.\", \"risk_notes\": [\"Lock order remains inconsistent (T0: A0 then A1; T1: A1 then A0) which could still cause deadlock if barrier timing allows interleaving after lock acquisition begins. However, the barrier now releases both threads simultaneously, increasing chance of concurrent lock attempts which may exacerbate order violation. Consider enforcing global lock order.\"]}","status":"SUCCESS","latency_ms":4661.783000017749,"input_tokens":2449,"output_tokens":714,"estimated_cost_usd":null,"verification_status":"FAILED","verification_reason":"The patch failed the configured verification campaign; inspect execution evidence.","verification_evidence":{"patch_hash":"4c2bb26be8081024d07fbd33d550e18fb5f748b0e674d656c833e6f1829279e5","patch_application":{"success":true,"files_changed":["main.c"],"rejected_paths":[],"error":null,"error_code":null,"repair_hint":null,"source_line":null,"patch_hash":"4c2bb26be8081024d07fbd33d550e18fb5f748b0e674d656c833e6f1829279e5"},"candidate_sources":{"main.c":"#include <pthread.h>\n#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdint.h>\n#include <assert.h>\n#include <stdatomic.h>\n#include \"stress.h\"\n\nstatic long accounts[2] = {1000, 1000};\nstatic int transfers;\nstatic pthread_mutex_t locks[2] = {PTHREAD_MUTEX_INITIALIZER, PTHREAD_MUTEX_INITIALIZER};\nstatic pthread_barrier_t ready;\nstatic void *worker(void *arg) {\n    int from = (int)(intptr_t)arg, to = 1-from;\n    long amount = from == 0 ? 100 : 50;\n    pthread_barrier_wait(&ready);\n    pthread_mutex_lock(&locks[from]); printf(\"T%d LOCK A%d\\n\", from, from